      ],
      "source": "https://www.worldatlas.com/cities/matlacha-florida.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Matlacha sits on a narrow point in Matlacha Pass, between Pine Island and Little Pine Island.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matlacha%2C_Florida",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Matlacha is an Old Florida fishing village known for its brightly colored art galleries, island boutiques, seafood restaurants, and traditional Floridian cottages.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matlacha%2C_Florida",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "WildChild Art Gallery, opened in 2000, showcases contemporary art in a historic fishing cottage at Matlacha's heart.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
